# Stacked Page Sections

App and marketing pages use a **stacked sheet** layout: a flat-bottom hero, then full-width sections that overlap upward with rounded tops. Each section is a layer above the one before it.

## Rules

1. **Hero (layer 0)** — `StackedPageHero` or `relative z-0`. No rounded bottom. No negative top margin.
2. **Following sections** — Use `StackedPageSection` from `@/components/layout/StackedPageSection` with incrementing `layer` (1, 2, 3… → `z-10`, `z-20`, `z-30`…).
3. **Overlap** — Always `-mt-8` and `rounded-t-[2rem]` on stacked sections (provided by the component).
4. **Backgrounds** — Each section needs a solid `bg-*` so the overlap reads clearly. Alternate tones when adjacent layers share content type (e.g. `bg-brand-900` / `bg-neutral-900`).
5. **Width** — Section backgrounds are full-width; content stays in `max-w-[650px] mx-auto` (inside the component).
6. **Do not** wrap multiple logical sections in one stacked container — one `StackedPageSection` per vertical block.

## Example

Reference: `pages/journal.tsx` (log), `pages/journal/home.tsx` (app home).

```tsx
import { StackedPageHero, StackedPageSection } from '@/components/layout/StackedPageSection';

<StackedPageHero className="bg-gradient-to-b from-neutral-900 to-brand-700">
  {/* hero content — flat bottom */}
</StackedPageHero>

<StackedPageSection layer={1} className="bg-brand-900 pb-20">
  {/* first content block */}
</StackedPageSection>

<StackedPageSection layer={2} className="bg-neutral-900 pb-[100px]">
  {/* second content block */}
</StackedPageSection>
```

## Inner cards

Rounded cards (`rounded-[24px]`, images, shadows) live **inside** a stacked section, not as the section shell itself.
